      "name": "coverage",
      "displayName": "coverage",
      "queryLines": [
        "SELECT * FROM workspace.default.v_coverage_gaps WHERE state_alpha IN ('IA', 'IL', 'IN', 'NE', 'MN')"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "pages": [
    {
      "name": "p_fail",
      "displayName": "1. Where it fails",
      "layout": [
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "text_1",
            "multilineTextboxSpec": {
              "lines": [
                "## Where does the trigger fail farmers?\n\n",
                "Each point is a Corn Belt county under its state's chosen trigger. Darker = higher miss rate (share of loss years with no payout = basis risk).\n\n",
                "**Read with care:** thresholds are set from the same years they are tested on, so miss rates are optimistic. Each county counts as one insured acre; dollar figures show the shape of the risk, not real exposure. Crop prices and the 25% payout share are illustrative (notebook 13).\n\n"
              ]
            }
          },
          "position": {
            "x": 0,
            "y": 0,
            "width": 4,
            "height": 4
          }
        },
        {
          "widget": {
            "name": "filter_2",
            "queries": [
              {
                "name": "f_crop_basis_risk_map",
                "query": {
                  "datasetName": "basis_risk_map",
                  "fields": [
